glowcap is an alpha library for capability-based networking and
Loam transactional storage and durable actors, licensed under Apache-2.0.
Glowcap LLC maintains it at
[glowcap-org/glowcap](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap).

The software version is `0.1.6` alpha. CapTP `1.0` names a wire protocol it
supports. [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/releases)
holds the downloads, and the
[changelog](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)
records changes and required upgrade steps.

Pin a release or commit. APIs, ABIs, and storage formats can change before
1.0, including in patch releases. Back up stored data before upgrading.
The [release policy](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/maintaining.md#release-status)
defines compatibility expectations. glowcap has not received an independent
security audit. [SECURITY.md](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/SECURITY.md)
defines the security posture and the private reporting process.

# Where to go next

- **[Start building]($link.page('start'))** installs the Zig package and makes
  a complete call, with routes to the C ABI and every binding.
- **[Choose a transport]($link.page('transports/choosing'))** compares
  identity, encryption, reachability, browser support, and interoperability.
- **[What you can depend on]($link.page('stability'))** separates recurring
  checks, on-demand checks, and behavior without check coverage.
- **[Performance]($link.page('performance'))** publishes throughput,
  allocation, footprint, transport, and binding measurements with their
  methods.

# Get help or contribute

Ask a question or report a problem in
[GitHub Issues](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/issues).
Include the release version or commit, your operating system, what you
tried, and what happened. Confusing instructions and interoperability
failures are worth reporting too. You do not need to bring a fix.
[Contributing](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)
explains how to run the project and send a fix. Contributions are welcome
with or without AI tools.

# Project records

The repository keeps the detailed project record: [what
ships](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/shipped.md), [known
limitations](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/boundaries.md),
the [milestones to 1.0](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/milestones.md),
and the [remaining work](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md).
The [vision](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/vision.md)
defines what 1.0 is aiming for. Accepted and superseded choices are recorded in the
[decision index](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/decisions/README.md).

